FEX port
========

Base: FEX_SHA in pins.env. scripts/06-fex-arm64ec.sh resets the checkout and
applies 0001..0011 in order; that stack is the source of truth. 0002 applies
inside the External/rpmalloc submodule, the rest at the top of the tree.

0001  dual-mapped JIT memory: code is written through the arena's RW alias;
      the TEB lives in x28 (FEX's STATE moves to x14); no raw Linux syscalls
      on Darwin (FEX_HOST_DARWIN); C++ exception state without x18 TLS
0002  rpmalloc: aligned reservations through VirtualAlloc2, 16 MB spans
0003  a thread's lookup cache is allocated (committed) at its first x86 block
0004  unaligned TSO loads and stores are checked inline (FEX_IOS)
0005  committed, readable pages outside FEX's executable ranges are decodable
0006  FEX's own VM calls skip Wine's ARM64EC memory notifications
0007  KITSUNE_FEX_CODE_MB sizes the dual-mapped code buffer (16..128 MB)
0008  call-ret stack guard pages are whole host pages (64 KB)
0009  lookup cache sized to about 24 MB per thread
0010  FEX debug-level log lines are dropped unless KITSUNE_FEX_DEBUGLOG is set
0011  superseded code buffers are purged, then freed after a 5 s grace period

06 builds with -DFEX_HOST_DARWIN -DFEX_IOS.
